        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-10-14T18:48:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>A possible exception might be made for an Arcade-style villain who comes with his own personal Environment deck full of deathtraps and other nastiness, and a villain deck full of environment manipulating effects.  OTOH, you could model that sort of thing through his villain deck as well, so it’s not vital.  You might also do that style of villain as one that doesn’t use a normal Environment deack at all, and instead include actual Environment cards in his villain deck so that hero-deck cards that look for Environment cards have something to target.</p>\n<p>Maybe Flying Buffalo would let you borrow the name Grimtooth for the villain?  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 8,
